# Names only, never values (docs/rulebooks/backend-rules.md, Security).
# The BFF reads these server-side; none of them may be NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed.
FITFORGE_API_BASE_URL=

# FITFORGE_SESSION_SECRET was here until feature 002 phase 7 and is deliberately gone.
# Feature 001 added it anticipating a sealed session cookie; plan.md D4 chose not to seal
# one — HttpOnly already stops script reads, and a sealed blob is exactly as replayable
# as the token it wraps. A named secret nobody uses invites someone to make it
# load-bearing later without a decision, so it is removed rather than left empty.
